1
00:05:02,307 --> 00:05:08,307
No hammer. No problem.

2
00:10:04,615 --> 00:10:10,615
Thor: Ragnarok is a action, adventure, science
fiction film directed by Taika Waititi.

3
00:15:06,923 --> 00:15:12,923
Thor is imprisoned on the other side of the universe and finds himself in a race against time to get back to Asgard to stop Ragnarok, the
destruction of his home-world and the end of Asgardian civilization, at the hands of a powerful new threat, the ruthless Hela.

4
00:20:09,230 --> 00:20:15,230
Thor, played by Chris Hemsworth.

5
00:25:11,538 --> 00:25:17,538
Bruce Banner / Hulk, played by Mark Ruffalo.

6
00:30:13,846 --> 00:30:19,846
Loki, played by Tom Hiddleston.

7
00:35:16,153 --> 00:35:22,153
Hela, played by Cate Blanchett.

8
00:40:18,461 --> 00:40:24,461
Heimdall, played by Idris Elba.

9
00:45:20,769 --> 00:45:26,769
Grandmaster, played by Jeff Goldblum.

10
00:50:23,076 --> 00:50:29,076
Thor: Ragnarok is a 2017 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics character Thor,
produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures.

11
00:55:25,384 --> 00:55:31,384
It is the sequel to Thor (2011) and Thor: The Dark World (2013), and is
the 17th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

12
01:00:27,692 --> 01:00:33,692
The film was directed by Taika Waititi from a screenplay by Eric Pearson and the writing team of Craig Kyle and Christopher Yost, and stars Chris Hemsworth
as Thor alongside Tom Hiddleston, Cate Blanchett, Idris Elba, Jeff Goldblum, Tessa Thompson, Karl Urban, Mark Ruffalo, and Anthony Hopkins.

13
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:36,000
In Thor: Ragnarok, Thor must escape the alien planet Sakaar in time to save
Asgard from Hela (Blanchett) and the impending Ragnarök.

14
01:10:32,307 --> 01:10:38,307
A third Thor film was confirmed in January 2014, when
Kyle and Yost began work on the screenplay.

15
01:15:34,615 --> 01:15:40,615
The involvement of Hemsworth and Hiddleston was announced that October, and the
film's title was revealed to be Thor: Ragnarok later that month.

16
01:20:36,923 --> 01:20:42,923
Waititi joined the film as director a year later, after Thor: The
Dark World director Alan Taylor chose not to return.

17
01:25:39,230 --> 01:25:45,230
Ruffalo joined the cast reprising the role of Bruce Banner / Hulk from previous MCU films, which
allowed elements of the 2006 comic storyline "Planet Hulk" to be adapted for Ragnarok.

18
01:30:41,538 --> 01:30:47,538
The rest of the cast, including Blanchett as Hela, was confirmed in May 2016, with
Pearson's involvement revealed at the start of filming that July.

19
01:35:43,846 --> 01:35:49,846
Principal photography took place in Brisbane and Sydney, Australia, with the film also having
exclusive use of Village Roadshow Studios in Oxenford, concluding in October 2016.

20
01:40:46,153 --> 01:40:52,153
Thor: Ragnarok premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on October 10, 2017, and
was released in the United States on November 3, as part of Phase Three of the MCU.

21
01:45:48,461 --> 01:45:54,461
The film received praise for its acting and Waititi's direction, as well as the action sequences, visual effects,
musical score, and humor, with many critics considering it to be the best installment of the Thor franchise.

22
01:50:50,769 --> 01:50:56,769
It grossed $855 million, becoming the highest-grossing film of the
series and the ninth-highest-grossing film of 2017.

23
01:55:53,076 --> 01:55:59,076
A sequel, Thor: Love and Thunder, was released in July 2022.

24
02:00:55,384 --> 02:01:01,384
The film explores themes of superhero, based on comic,
sequel, alien planet, female villain.

25
02:05:57,692 --> 02:06:03,692
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
